plank-player (5.27.80+git20261005.f87e775-1+stereo3d1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show a stereoscopic 3D video to both eyes: Qt Multimedia's stereo mode of
    the frames (every packing of H.264 Table D-8 and RFC 9559, either eye
    first) read by a StereoFilter, the two views in a layer under the window
    declared to the compositor as full side by side, the on-screen display
    and menus a 2D surface the same in both eyes; elsewhere the left view.
  * A 3D menu on the on-screen display (remote control): the view, the input
    format for a video that does not declare it, Swap Eyes; a video that says
    nothing and is at least 2.5 times as wide as high is taken as full size
    views side by side.
  * Do not activate a button twice on Return (Bigscreen.Button handles it, and
    so did MenuButton and OSDButton: play/pause paused and resumed at once).
  * Depend on libqt6multimedia6 and qml6-module-qtmultimedia
    (>= 6.11.2-3+stereo3d2~) and on libstereo-declare1.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0300

plank-player (5.27.80+git20261005.f87e775-1~sparky1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package KDE's Plank Player from the master branch of
    invent.kde.org/plasma/plank-player at f87e775 (not in Debian; its last
    tarball is the Plasma 5 5.27.12, and master is the Qt 6 port at version
    5.27.80), unchanged, built against Qt Multimedia 6.11.2-3+stereo3d2.

